{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1539479-weigthed-tag-and-forceful-martial-arts","id":1539479,"title":"Weigthed Tag and Forceful Martial Arts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-07-29T08:54:44-07:00","id":1539479,"title":"Weigthed Tag and Forceful Martial Arts","content":"Hi!<br /> <br /> Mostly having a lot of problems following well this game. I wanted to know if there is an errata or something I'm not taking into account with the Wigthed Tag and, in consequence, the Forceful Martial Arts Edge<br /> <br /> Knockdown is a (1s) Stunt<br /> <br /> Weigthed gives you a reduction of <b>two</b> to this 1s Stunt, and you can stack it with Forceful Martial Arts for reducing by <b>four</b> this 1s Stunt but &quot;you need at least 1s&quot;<br /> <br /> I haven't seen <i>any</i> way to upgrade Knockdown to a 5s Stunt for this to be viable<br /> <br /> I haven't seen <i>yet</i> any way to upgrade Knowdown to a 2s to begin with<br /> <br /> So, what is the interaction/intention here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27384-altidiya","name":"altidiya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-29T16:11:11-07:00","id":1539506,"title":"","content":"I've always played that the reduction makes the knockdown free. I also use a house rule where Mega-Might, and cat like balance increase the difficulty for knockdown. Also, there may be a gift that increases the cost of knockdown. I may be miss remembering, it might be in Adventure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-30T00:00:31-07:00","id":1539518,"title":"","content":"My house rules books has the following replacement for the Weighted tag:<br /> <br /> Weighted (1): This tag grants 2 enhancements that can be used only with the Knock Down/Trip and Shove Stunts.<br /> <br /> And the following change for the Shove stunt<br /> <br /> Shove (1 success): This stunt pushes the target back 1 range band away from the character. This stunt can be bought additional times, one extra for every scale the attack have above the target size, stacking the number of range bands the target is pushed.<br /> <br /> With Forceful Martial Arts I would let those extras enhancements to be split among many targets, so you can shove 4 guys away for free if you hit them all, for example, or shove and knock down 2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-30T07:20:42-07:00","id":1539526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1539479-weigthed-tag-and-forceful-martial-arts?p=1539518#post1539518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My house rules books has the following replacement for the Weighted tag:<br /> <br /> Weighted (1): This tag grants 2 enhancements that can be used only with the Knock Down/Trip and Shove Stunts.<br /> <br /> And the following change for the Shove stunt<br /> <br /> Shove (1 success): This stunt pushes the target back 1 range band away from the character. This stunt can be bought additional times, one extra for every scale the attack have above the target size, stacking the number of range bands the target is pushed.<br /> <br /> With Forceful Martial Arts I would let those extras enhancements to be split among many targets, so you can shove 4 guys away for free if you hit them all, for example, or shove and knock down 2.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thankiu<br /> <br /> I will see if I have the money to check that houserules book, they seem to perfect this system","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27384-altidiya","name":"altidiya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}